<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2585" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">angustĭo</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		angustus, pr. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to make narrow</i>, <i>to
			straiten;</i> only trop. and in eccl. Lat. <i>to
				straiten</i>, <i>hamper</i>, <i>distress</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">angustiatus prae pavore,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Jud. 13, 29</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">qui se angustiaverunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. Sap.
					5, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sed non angustiamur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 2
					Cor. 4, 8</span></i>
			; 6, 12; <i><span class="en">ib. Heb. 11, 37</span></i>.</div>
